meta {
  name: Analyze Clean Setup
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/llm/analyze/SPY?timeframe=M5&session=RTH&fact=Swift Trend flipped BULLISH 3 bars ago&fact=ADX 28 and rising&fact=Price 0.4 ATR above the Supertrend line and separation widening&fact=No scheduled news in next 30 minutes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timeframe: M5
  session: RTH
  fact: Swift Trend flipped BULLISH 3 bars ago
  fact: ADX 28 and rising
  fact: Price 0.4 ATR above the Supertrend line and separation widening
  fact: No scheduled news in next 30 minutes
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # LLM Analyze — Clean Bullish Setup

  Runs the local-LLM advisory analyst over a hand-built signal briefing and
  returns its verdict. INSPECTION ONLY — it does NOT place orders and does NOT
  read live market data; you pass the signal facts directly so you can probe any
  scenario and watch how the model scores it.

  Requires `app.llm.enabled=true` and a reachable local runtime (Ollama by
  default at http://localhost:11434 running the configured model, e.g. qwen3:8b).

  ## Path
  - `{ticker}` — any symbol label (free text; need not be in the watchlist).

  ## Query
  - `timeframe` — the timeframe the facts describe (default M5).
  - `session`   — market session label (default RTH).
  - `fact`      — REPEATABLE. Each occurrence is one plain-language signal fact.
                  Add/remove `fact` lines to change the briefing.

  ## Response (200)
  { ticker, timeframe, session, facts[], model, llmEnabled,
    verdict: { action (ENTER|WAIT|SKIP), conviction (1..maxConviction),
               rationale, riskFlags[], ok, note },
    timestamp }

  - `ok=true`  → a trusted, parsed model verdict.
  - `ok=false` → fail-safe WAIT (LLM disabled/down/slow/bad output); `note`
    explains why. The verdict is advisory — the risk/exit layer keeps final say.

  This request is the "clean setup": a fresh bullish flip with a rising ADX and
  widening separation. Expect ENTER with a high conviction.
}
